# Finishing Suite house style

Docker-hosted web apps in this family share one visual system. Vanity Hop (`io.thefinish.ing`) is the reference. Do not invent a new palette, a light theme, or a different control style. Branding settings may override the colour tokens at runtime; the defaults below stay the starting point.

## Colour and type

```css
:root {
  --bg: #0b0c0e;
  --surface: #141518;
  --ink: #e6e6dc;
  --muted: #aaaaa4;
  --line: #2a2b32;
  --accent: #a62525;
  --button-text: #e6e6dc;
  --error: #ff8b7b;
  --ok: #8ee0b1;
  --bg-image-opacity: 0.28;
  --ui: "Avenir Next", "Segoe UI", system-ui, sans-serif;
}
```

Page text is 15px, line-height 1.45, left-aligned. Headings are weight 600, letter-spacing -0.03em. `h1` is 1.5rem. Labels are 0.8rem in `--muted`.

Set `font-size: 15px` on `body` only. Do not set it on `html`. The root stays 16px, and `rem` is based on that root, so a 36rem sheet is 576px on every app. Setting 15px on the root shrinks the sheet to 540px.

## Page

- Column: `min(960px, calc(100% - 32px))`, centred, padded 24px above and 72px below.
- A background image, when set, sits on a fixed layer at `--bg-image-opacity` (default 0.28). The page background stays `--bg`.
- Centred sheets (login, settings forms, branding): surface fill, 1px `--line` border, 14px radius, 24px padding, max-width 36rem.
- Lists span the column. Each item is its own rounded row (12px radius, 8px gap), not a full-width underline list. Hover uses `--accent`.

## Header

Brand on the left: the logo if one is set, otherwise the brand name in weight 700. The logo is 28px tall.

Once signed in, the right side is the signed-in name, then navigation, then logout. The name is in `--muted`, with a divider on its right. Navigation and logout stay `--muted` until hover.

A logged-out page keeps the same header and shows nothing on the right.

## Login

Match Vanity Hop's logged-out screen.

- Same page column and header. No navigation.
- One centred sheet, max-width 36rem.
- When a logo is set, repeat it inside the sheet at 36px tall, above the heading.
- Heading is **Log in**. Do not use the product name as the heading. No lede under it.
- Then the credential fields the app actually needs. Vanity Hop asks for a password only. An app with accounts asks for username, then password.
- Primary button label is **Continue**.
- Document title is `Log in · {brand}`.

## Controls

- Primary button: `--accent` background, `--button-text`, 8px radius. Hover is `color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 82%, black)`.
- Secondary actions and text buttons use `--muted` until hover, with no filled background.
- Inputs: `--bg` fill, 1px `--line` border, 8px radius, 10px 12px padding, full width of the sheet.
- Dropdowns are ordinary `select` elements. Every page loads `/static/menu.js`, which replaces the operating-system menu with a page-drawn list. The highlighted row uses `--accent` and `--button-text`. Do not leave a dropdown on the system popup, and do not build a separate menu for one screen.
- Errors use `--error`. Success uses `--ok`.

## Settings

Subpages, in this order: Users & Scope, then Branding.

Branding, when the app has it: name, background, surface, text, muted text, borders, accent, button text, logo, favicon, background image, background strength (default 0.28), Save branding, and Reset branding. No light/dark toggle.
